.nh
.TH "PB-SEND-CANCEL" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-send-cancel - Cancel a file transfer batch


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb send cancel <transfer-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Cancel one outgoing transfer batch by its transfer ID. --on is required: name the machine
the files were sent to. The command prints the batch's resulting state; files that were already
delivered are not deleted.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for cancel

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--on\fP=""
	machine the files were sent to, by name or ID (required)

.PP
\fB--session\fP=""
	terminal session ID for destination context


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb send cancel transfer_abc --on laptop
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-send(1)\fP
